//     * Ref                - DocumentRef - Link to the current document.
//     * Invoice             - DocumentRef - Link to the invoice. If the current document is an order, it should
//                               be passed Undefined. The invoice passes a link to itself.
//     * OrderDocument                 - DocumentRef - Link to the order. If there are no such details, you should pass
//                               Undefined. The Order itself transmits a link to itself; the invoice
//                               cannot transmit a link to itself.
//     * Date                  - Date - Date of receipt / planned date of receipt of the product.
//     * Contract               - CatalogRef.CounterpartyContracts - Contract with the supplier, can be used
//                               as an access Document. If there are no such details, or if the document cannot
//                               be accepted under the contract, you should send it Undefined.
//     * Terms            - CatalogRef.TermsOfPurchaseFromVendors - Agreement with the supplier, can be used
//                               as an access Document. If there are no such details, or if the document cannot
//                               be accepted under the agreement, it should be passed Undefined.
//     * GoodsReceiptOption - EnumRef.GoodsReceiptOptions - the document's eponymous detail, if 
//                               there is no such detail, should be passed Undefined
//     * Warehouse                 - CatalogRef.Warehouses - The warehouse where the product will be delivered. 
//     * Sender           - DefinedType.SenderRecipientOfGoods - where the product is expected to arrive from.
//     * BusinessOperation - EnumRef.BusinessTransactions - eponymous document details.
//     * Products          - CatalogRef.Products - Nomenclature.
//     * Characteristic        - CatalogRef.ItemsCharacteristics - characteristic.
//     * Purpose            - CatalogRef.Assignments - purpose.
//     * ToControlQuality - Boolean - If the goods planned for admission are subject to quality control upon admission, then it is True, otherwise it is False.
//     * RecordOfAPreviouslyReceivedLot - Boolean - If the goods that were previously received and are under quality control are planned to be received, then it is True, otherwise it is False.
//     * ControlledLotReference - CatalogRef.ControlledLots - A link to a party that was received earlier (if the movement parameter of the party that received it = True), otherwise it is undefined or an empty link. 
//     * BatchesIndicationStatus   - Number - Service field of the table part, if there is no such detail, pass 0.
//     * ExceedingOrder           - Boolean - Service field for invoices, which is set to true if the invoice is for
//                               an order, and the line has a sign that it is not linked to the order, for example, line Code = 0.
//     * Series                 - CatalogRef.ItemsBatches - The series, if there are no such details, should be passed Undefined.
//     * Count            - Number - Quantity.
//     * ReceiptUnderOrders  - Boolean - Indicates that the current document is an order invoice.
//     * ThisIsAnInvoice          - Boolean - Indicates that the current document is an invoice.
//  SynonymForDocumentTable - String - Synonym of the main table in the text of the document Request, if different from
//                                     the default value.
//  ServicesAndWorksAreCountedInRegisteredRecords - Boolean - A sign that works and services should be taken into account in the movements
//
